{
  "summary": "SOX Protocol web app: a static React 18 + Vite SPA that consumes the TypeScript SDK against the SOX HTTP transport. Renders channels, message threads, agent presence, and a compose bar over watch()-driven live updates. Distributed twice: as @sox-protocol/ui on npm/CDN for the public demo, and bundled into the Python wheel under sox_protocol/ui_assets/ where a new `sox ui` CLI subcommand boots the HTTP transport, opens a browser, and serves the static bundle from /ui/.",
  "stack": {
    "framework": "React 18 + Vite (decided — docs/decisions/webapp-deployment-model.md)",
    "state": "Zustand",
    "styling": "Tailwind"
  },
  "deployment": {
    "model": "Static SPA bundled into Python wheel; served by sox HTTP transport at /ui/ (decided — docs/decisions/webapp-deployment-model.md)",
    "distribution": [
      "npm package @sox-protocol/ui for standalone/CDN use",
      "packages/python/src/sox_protocol/ui_assets/ bundled into wheel"
    ],
    "rationale": "See docs/decisions/webapp-deployment-model.md — pure static + permissive CORS on HTTP transport gives one artifact for both the public demo (CDN) and local UX (sox ui), without a Node proxy."
  },
